@startuml
' Figure - Use Case Diagram: system overview
!include _header.txt
left to right direction

actor "Read-Only Auditor" as RO
actor "Forensic Analyst"  as ANA
actor "Lead Investigator" as LEAD
actor "Administrator"     as ADM

' Specialisation: the Auditor is the MOST GENERAL actor. Each actor below
' specialises the one above it and therefore inherits its associations.
ANA  --|> RO
LEAD --|> ANA
ADM  --|> LEAD

rectangle DEICMS {
  usecase "Review case records\n(23 use cases)"      as P1
  usecase "Examine and handle evidence\n(+2)"        as P2
  usecase "Manage investigations\n(+7)"              as P3
  usecase "Administer the system\n(+9)"              as P4
}

RO   --> P1
ANA  --> P2
LEAD --> P3
ADM  --> P4

note bottom of DEICMS
  41 use cases in total, one per system operation.
  Each actor is joined only to the use cases it ADDS;
  the rest are inherited through specialisation.
  Totals: Auditor 23, Analyst 25, Lead 32, Administrator 41.
  Detail follows in the three diagrams after this one.
end note
@enduml
